+# finding, D-015): `DispatchRegistry` is only written *after* the exec
+# worker's `tasks show` poll first confirms the record is visible, while the
+# MCP events_wait loop starts listening earlier — for a task phrased so
+# tersely it finishes within that same couple of seconds (e.g. "reply ok"),
+# the terminal event can race ahead of the registry write and get silently
+# dropped (known timing gap, tracked as debt D-015, not fixed by this task).
+# The task below asks for a short written explanation (~200 Chinese
+# characters) — long enough, empirically (~6-10s wall time for this
+# project's local gateway), to clear that window; see backend-notes.md for
+# the measured margin.
